Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:29:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] FP fold kill proofs: a Call is an opaque reader of
 xmm0-xmm7

Red-team audit of PRs #363/#364 (delta da964ed4..77eb34e1): the
is_cf_transfer straight-line rule is correct, but two of the three folds
lacked the call veto the commit message claimed all three have, and the
stated justification ("a call clobbers every caller-saved xmm") misses
the real hazard: the call itself reads %xmm0-%xmm7 implicitly as the
SysV FP argument registers, and the self-move-elided argument staging
leaves no textual trace.

- fold_fp_register_loads: refuse the kill when a Call lies in the
  (consumer, overwrite) stretch and the loaded register is xmm0-xmm7.
- fold_zero_addend_fma213_to_132: same veto (b <= 7) in the ok_after
  scan; xmm0 is the zeroing register itself, excluded by construction.
- xmm8-xmm15 keep scanning: callee-saved, never argument registers,
  never read before definition by compiled code.
- is_cf_transfer doc + fold_fma_memory_src2 comments: precise wording.
- 6 tests (2 refusals verified red on unfixed upstream, 4 positive
  controls).  Reachability analysis + 192-function empirical sweep in
  engineering/AUDIT-2026-09-03-pr363-364-fp-fold-call-veto.md: latent
  (per-use constant materialization, call-free hoist gate), fixed as
  defense in depth.

units 1670/0/6; suite PASS=570 FAIL=0 SKIP=15 AB-diff 0.
