From c0cf9ad4b6cf5bdd4ff0554751a4884804b51f17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:26:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Typed 128-bit pair store/load: Mov128 closes
 Store(other)/Load(other)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The census's largest MachInst-actionable class: i128 pair stores went
through the accumulator + spill + relay path (7 instrs + 16B dead frame
traffic where every godbolt oracle uses 2), loads mirrored.

Three typed forms, cheapest first:
- Const: two S64 Movs at the destination halves (imm32 window or the
  hardened wide-imm relay; no staging, no spill, no pool entry).
- Value: the new atomic MachInst::Mov128 — movdqu load + movdqu store
  through the pre-colored xmm0 scratch, data-dependent so overlapping
  regions stay correct.  movdqu, never movdqa: frame slots sit at 8
  mod 16 and packed-member alignment is untracked (measured).
- Scratch-unsafe: four S64 Movs through the reserved rax/rdx, both
  loads before either store.

Two soundness gates, both suite-caught or probe-proven:
- state.is_i128_value excludes the I128-typed VECTOR alias whose spill
  slot is lazily written (builtin_ia32_vector_value: zeroed upper lanes).
- Store vals need COHERENT homes (prologue fixpoint: i128 ParamRefs,
  128-bit call results, propagated through Copy and i128 Load dests) —
  a value living in the accumulator pair has a slot whose only writer
  would be the store itself.

Volatile, segment overrides, over-aligned allocas, folded addresses and
indexed addressing keep the mature path.

Census: Store(other) 79 -> 0, Load(other) 7 -> 0; coverage 48.85% ->
49.06%.  Oracle scoreboard (gcc 15.2/16.2, clang 23.1.0, icc 2021.10,
icx latest) in engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-03b-typed-i128-pair.md.
Tests: 7 isel/emitter stress tests + assembler-corpus Mov128 coverage +
tests/regression/i128_pair_store_load.c runtime oracle.

